/E (A liquidity sweep happens when price runs above a swing high or below a swing low, triggering stop orders before reversing direction. Those stops \(the automatic exit points of traders already in the market\) act as pools of liquidity. When price hits them, it gives the market the fuel it needs to move the other way.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
